 "protocol": {
  "summary": "As principal-displacement test; Table 3 reports all 6 motion components at 400 N compression and 145 N shear.",
  "how_to_simulate": [
   "Fix the inferior vertebra; leave the superior vertebra free; output = displacement of the centre of the superior vertebral body",
   "Compression: apply 400 N axial force in 100 N steps (report 86, 145 and 400 N)",
   "Shear: with the 400 N compressive preload, apply horizontal anterior, posterior or right-lateral force at the level of the superior vertebral body centre (3.4 cm above the disc centre) in steps to 145 N",
   "Report all 6 motion components of the superior vertebral body centre at 145 N shear / 400 N compression; compare sign and magnitude (shear is coupled with flexion/extension/lateral bending because the shear acts 3.4 cm above the disc centre)"
  ],
  "subject_model": null,
  "notes": "Coordinate/reference: Inferior vertebra clamped, superior fixture unconstrained; displacements and rotations of the centre of the SUPERIOR vertebral body (6 dial gauges). Shear dead weights applied horizontally near the centre of the superior vertebral body, i.e. acting on the disc centre through a mean moment arm of 3.4 cm (shear is therefore accompanied by a bending moment of ~0.034 m x F). Sign convention as printed: positive = left, posterior, superior translation; flexion, left lateral bend, CCW torsion. No SD reported."
 },
